---
import BaseHead from "../components/BaseHead.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { SITE_TITLE, SITE_DESCRIPTION } from "../consts";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Header />
    <main>
      <p>
        This is a blog about the small things. Not frameworks, not paradigms, not the next big
        thing. Just the pieces — a shell one-liner that saves a minute every day, the git flag you
        always look up, the kind of detail you either know or spend half an afternoon rediscovering.
      </p>
      <p>
        Posts tend to be short. Subjects tend to be narrow. The goal is something worth reading in
        under five minutes — concrete, something you can actually use. If it saves a lookup, a Stack
        Overflow spiral, three rounds of rephrasing the same question to ChatGPT, or an hour of
        frustration, that's enough.
      </p>
      <p>
        Software engineering has plenty of complexity. Most of it is necessary. Some of it is just
        unfamiliarity with the right tool at the right moment. That's the gap this tries to fill.
      </p>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>
